## Lore

The New Luftwaffe takes its pilots from the NGR Army''s bravest aviators.
Candidates are tested on flying, gargoyle tactics and aviation history, and
quietly screened for stability and loyalty. Fewer than a third are accepted,
and about half of those turn the offer down once they hear it means a full
cybernetic reconstruction.

Those who accept become light full conversion cyborgs whose bodies plug into
an XML series airframe. Lying prone inside it, the pilot feels the aircraft as
his own body: its sensors are his senses, its weapons fire like a thrown
punch, and damage to the wings registers as something done to him. Their
reactions are many times faster than a human pilot''s, and they fly low,
fast and close in ways no flesh pilot survives.

Most come to love it, and many become thrill seekers who take risks they
cannot see. Away from the cockpit they grow bored or anxious, so the
Luftwaffe keeps them flying fourteen hours or more a day and lets them rest in
calming sleep berths. So far they have avoided the depression and
dissociation other full conversion cyborgs suffer, but the program is only a
few years old.

## GM Notes

The NGR keeps the program secret; even its allies are not told what the
pilots are. Pilots are paid 2,500 credits a month (4,000-5,000 at 8th level
and up), live in private apartments with food, clothing and bionic
maintenance provided, start as lieutenants and usually hold mid to top level
security clearance.
